/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/redteam/directives/stage_099.md:79:All four `R_n - (N_Q - 1) == 0` assertions in both engines are guaranteed by the script's own construction. In sympy, `K_n = N_Q * K_n_target` makes `R_n = K_n/K_n_target - 1 = N_Q - 1` identically; for `Gamma_5 = 9 K_2^{5/2}/K_0^{3/2}`, the same multiplicative `N_Q` cancellation gives `R_5 = N_Q^{5/2}/N_Q^{3/2} - 1 = N_Q - 1` identically. In Mathematica, `kbar = nQ*k0Target*yhatCons` followed by series extraction reproduces the same per-construction reductions (`Coefficient[nQ*X*yhatCons, omega, 2n] = nQ * Coefficient[X*yhatCons, omega, 2n] = nQ * k_n_target`). No assertion can fail.
