/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/redteam/tmp_prompts/audit_directive_115.md:31:The `.wl` script is a line-by-line rewrite of `scripts/moving_throat_pde_stage115_core_balance_compensation_sympy_audit.py:24-70`. Every algebraic step, the branch pick (`First[gQSolutions]` vs `gq_solutions[0]`), and the substitution sequence are identical. There is no independent derivation of the balance surface or of `sigma_c = sigma_*` in the Mathematica script — it merely echoes the SymPy algebra in Mathematica notation. The second-engine policy requires an independent algebraic route. The Part-IV appendix (`paper/appendices/stage_appendix_part04.tex` lines 530-543) supplies one: the parent-overlap reparametrization `mathfrak r = lambda/sqrt(K_s K_q)`, `mathfrak g = g_q sqrt(K_s)/(g_s sqrt(K_q))` with the equivalent compensation family `1 + mathfrak r^2 = 4 (mathfrak g - mathfrak r)^2` and roots `mathfrak g_+- = mathfrak r +- (1/2) sqrt(1 + mathfrak r^2)`.
