/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/redteam/tmp_prompts/audit_directive_126.md:70:The paper card's `Checks` enumerates "Check positivity of the mouth source; do not use signed fitting to reach the upper branch." (paper/stages/stage_126.tex:22). The notes also state "This is normalized and nonnegative on `[0,L]`" (notes line 78). The scripts define `sigma_match = k*cos(k*z)` and `sigma_xi = (1-xi)*k*cos(k*z) + xi/L`, then check normalization and Family-1 compensation, but never assert nonnegativity. Without an assertion, a future regression that introduces a sign-changing source would not be caught — defeating the stage's load-bearing positivity claim.
/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/redteam/tmp_prompts/audit_directive_119.md:105:Section IV's banner is "Explicit traction law", but the two `T_m` branch solutions are only `print`ed; no assertion ties the script output to the notes (§5) boxed form `T_m = sqrt(2 Z_q K_s) / (J_s c_s sqrt(μ₀ L_W)) · 1 / (r̂ ± (1/2) sqrt(1 + r̂²))`. The literal target form (after factor-of-2 rearrangement) is `2 sqrt(2 Z_q K_s) / (J_s c_s sqrt(μ₀ L_W) (2 r̂ ± sqrt(1 + r̂²)))`, which matches the current printed SymPy output exactly.
/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/redteam/tmp_prompts/audit_directive_119.md:128:The Mathematica `tMPlus` and `tMMinus` outputs are wrapped in `ConditionalExpression[..., condition]` (see saved transcript lines 39-40). The existing `expectZero` helper applies `FullSimplify[Together[Expand[expr]]]` and then `TrueQ[res === 0]`, but `ConditionalExpression` will survive simplification, so a direct subtraction will not reduce to `0`. Strip `ConditionalExpression` heads before comparison.
